 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The condition of the real hypothetical period (type 1)",
     "texto": [
      "To state certain, probable or immediate conditions, use: **Se + present indicative, present indicative**: **Se piove, resto a casa** (if it rains, I stay at home); **Se fa freddo, metto la sciarpa** (if it's cold, I put on my scarf).",
      "It is also very common to combine **se + present** with a consequence in the **simple future**: **Se fa bel tempo domani, andremo al mare** (if the weather is nice tomorrow, we'll go to the seaside)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Alternative and disjunctive connectors",
     "texto": [
      "**Altrimenti** (otherwise / or else): *Prendi l'ombrello, altrimenti ti bagni* (take the umbrella, otherwise you'll get wet). **Quindi** (therefore / so): *Piove, quindi restiamo qui* (it's raining, so we're staying here)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Real condition patterns",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Protasis (condition with se)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Apodosis (result or plan)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Meaning",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
